    "published": true,
    "description": "Based on the conceptual understanding developed in the previous activity on displacement and vector resolution, this assessment requires students to independently apply those principles to a mission-based problem. Students will interpret the rover’s final distress signal, resolve the given displacement into horizontal and vertical components using trigonometric relations, and accurately plot the rover’s position on a Cartesian grid. They will then demonstrate applied understanding by navigating the drone along the most efficient vector path to the target. This assessment evaluates conceptual clarity, accuracy of calculations, graphical representation skills, and the ability to translate theoretical knowledge into precise, energy-efficient execution under realistic constraints",
